From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 12 Jul 2026 08:45:46 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 06866/11362] [outer-loop] ARC lf52: document 3x timeout
 pattern (round-3 leg), no artifact

Three consecutive codex sessions targeting lf52's L5 (1800s, 2400s, then a
3000s relaunch) all timed out before writing any artifact -- every session
spent its budget building an interactive PNG-rendering driver harness
before real exploration started. No mechanic knowledge gained; this is a
session-startup-overhead problem specific to this game's exploration
workflow, not a finding about the game. Frontier stays at level 4.
No registry count change.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JntPrUGLNesPcJH1pyfFYw
---
 ops/arc_solve_registry.yaml | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/ops/arc_solve_registry.yaml b/ops/arc_solve_registry.yaml
index 7ad514325c..7e530343a5 100644
--- a/ops/arc_solve_registry.yaml
+++ b/ops/arc_solve_registry.yaml
@@ -2108,6 +2108,19 @@ games:
     reset+remap+verify pass could not fit). A large "keyhole" reset structure
     was also found (clicking it resets L5) -- distinct from the peg-stranding
     auto-reset.'
+  - 'INFRA NOTE round 3 (2026-07-12, gpt-5.6-sol via codex, round-3 breadth
+    campaign): three consecutive codex sessions targeting this game''s L5
+    (1800s, 2400s, then a 3000s relaunch) all TIMED OUT before writing any
+    artifact -- every session spent its budget building an interactive
+    PNG-rendering driver harness to visualize the board before real
+    exploration started, rather than reusing a lighter-weight approach.
+    No new mechanic knowledge was gained in any of the three attempts (all
+    three died mid-tooling-setup); this is a session-startup-overhead
+    problem specific to this game''s exploration workflow, not a finding
+    about the game itself. Frontier stays at level 4. Next attempt should
+    skip the PNG-rendering step entirely and reason from raw grid arrays
+    (as most other games'' sessions do) to leave more budget for actual L5
+    exploration.'
